.MARINE...
(Today through Sunday)
Issued at 1033 AM PDT Tue Sep 29 2026

Strong high pressure off the California Coast will result in fresh
to near gale northerly breezes through Wednesday over the coastal
waters. Frequent gale force gusts are expected across the
northern waters through Wednesday morning. Conditions will begin
to improve Wednesday night as northerly breezes diminish to become
gentle to moderate, with locally hazardous conditions across the
northern outer waters likely to continue. Rough to very rough seas
through Wednesday will subside to become moderate to rough.

