.FIRE WEATHER...
Issued at 515 AM PDT Mon Sep 28 2026

The marine layer persists this morning, around 1500-2000ft, but
should gradually compress to around 500ft throughout the day.
Today will be coolest day of the week, though it is also the start
of a warming trend. Offshore flow gradually works its way into the
region today, which will lead to breezy winds each morning from through
Wednesday. The strongest winds are expected on Tuesday morning in
the interior mountains of the North and East Bays, where wind
gusts could reach 30-35 mph. These offshore winds should
contribute to poor overnight humidity recoveries, with overnight
relative humidities as low as 20-40% above the marine layer.

